  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Skies over Nevada range from clear to \npartly cloudy tonight as upper level ridging continues to dictate \nour weather patterns. The ridge is forecast to persist through \nFriday when a trough and associated atmospheric river break it. \nUntil then, high temperatures will be in the upper 50s and low 60s\nwhile overnight lows drop into the 30s. The usual cold valleys \nmay see lows drop into the upper 20s. Winds will be light during \nthis period, less than 10 mph. As the trough approaches on Friday \nwinds are expected to pick up, with gusts approaching 30 mph \nmainly in northern Nevada Friday afternoon. Wind gusts are \nexpected to remain around 30 mph while the trough is over Nevada. \nAdditionally, the AR moisture is forecast to produce \nprecipitation, currently forecast to begin as rain Saturday \nevening and transition to mostly snow by Monday morning as \ntemperatures drop. High temperatures are currently expected to \nonly reach the 30s on Monday, although this weather system is \nstill in flux and timing, track and intensity all may change as \nmodel agreement improves.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in continued\nridging through late week. Moderate confidence in troughing this\nweekend but low confidence in its strength and impacts. No changes\nfrom NBM forecast.",
